==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|orð|lang=non}} < {{proto|Germanic|wurða-|lang=is}} < {{proto|Indo-European|werdho-|word|lang=is}} < {{proto|Indo-European|wer-|speak|lang=is}}. Cognate with Old Frisian {{term||word}}, Old Saxon {{term||word|lang=osx}} (Dutch {{term|woord|lang=nl}}), Old High German {{term|wort|lang=goh}} (German {{term|Wort|lang=de}}), Swedish {{term|ord|lang=sv}}) and Gothic {{term|sc=Goth|𐍅𐌰𐌿𐍂𐌳|tr=waurd|lang=got}}.

The Proto-Indo-European root is also the source of Latin {{term|verbum|lang=la}}, Lithuanian {{term|vardas|lang=lt}}, and, more distantly, of Ancient Greek {{term|sc=polytonic|εἴρω|tr=eirō||I say|lang=grc}} and Old Church Slavonic {{term|ротити|ротити сѧ|tr=rotiti sę|to swear|lang=cu|sc=Cyrs}} (Russian {{term|sc=Cyrl|ротиться|tr=rotit’sja||to vow|lang=ru}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ɔrð/|lang=is}}

===Noun===
'''orð''' {{n}} ([[orðs|orð-s]], [[#Icelandic|orð-]])

# [[word]]
#: '''Orðið''' "[[slagharpa]]" er [[gamall|gamalt]] '''orð'''.
#:: The '''word''' "[[pianoforte]]" is an [[old]] '''word'''.
# [[remarks]]
# [[request]]
# [[message]]
# [[promise]], one's [[word]]
#: ''Að [[halda orð sín|halda '''orð''' sín]].''
#:: To [[keep one's word]].
# [[reputation]]
#: ''Frambjóðandinn hefur á sér gott '''orð'''.''
#:: The candidate has a good '''reputation'''.

